{"id": "EUVD-2026-58992", "enisaUuid": "3707fa2c-c38e-33dd-9cb5-da7e906262fb", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfhandle: reject detached mounts in capable_wrt_mount()\n\nThe recent fhandle RCU fix moved the mount namespace capability check\ninto capable_wrt_mount(), so a non-NULL mnt_namespace survives the\nns_capable() dereference. The helper still assumes the later\nREAD_ONCE(mount->mnt_ns) must be non-NULL because may_decode_fh()\nchecked is_mounted() first.\n\nThat assumption is not stable. A detached mount from\nopen_tree(..., OPEN_TREE_CLONE) can be dissolved on fput while\nopen_by_handle_at() is between those checks, and umount_tree() can\nclear mount->mnt_ns. If the helper observes NULL, it dereferences\nmnt_ns->user_ns and panics.\n\nReturn false when the RCU read observes a detached mount. This keeps\nthe relaxed permission path conservative: a mount no longer attached\nto a namespace cannot authorize open_by_handle_at() access.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:51:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T21:19:23", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/15104234c267ebe04b9f9a73e5c2179cc265ff60", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6c52226072a3c61337b1eec1799bb987748884fa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6ee183d89261bf1d1cf9f06d80a40dab8f36ee55", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6c732471740bc2ac9b0946134f9f551dc75f4369"], "aliases": ["GHSA-g7v4-chcg-vj96", "CVE-2026-72034"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "256c4a20-4fd0-3ac3-8609-de794b30513a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.97"}, {"id": "32f33485-82d9-3e4b-b999-02dd7c9d1868", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "620c266f394932e5decc4b34683a75dfc59dc2f4 <6ee183d89261bf1d1cf9f06d80a40dab8f36ee55"}, {"id": "8940f3a8-803d-3b07-adef-7eeb3ba02c19", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.11"}, {"id": "dc33c0a3-21a6-3b8c-b6f9-00667e611193", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "df6e7127-3a8a-3e93-b1e8-234e520bc872", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "ed1f7e28-d104-3707-94cf-82fe6a6f56ba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "620c266f394932e5decc4b34683a75dfc59dc2f4 <6c732471740bc2ac9b0946134f9f551dc75f4369"}, {"id": "ee4059bb-cc13-385e-854f-31361012b652", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "f2edda54-ba4f-34e4-891d-cd4db4ea624f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "f2f13291-8398-3e39-b480-0c04e0b57f2a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "620c266f394932e5decc4b34683a75dfc59dc2f4 <6c52226072a3c61337b1eec1799bb987748884fa"}, {"id": "fcdabad6-961f-3ce2-a1ac-361d13cbd108", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "620c266f394932e5decc4b34683a75dfc59dc2f4 <15104234c267ebe04b9f9a73e5c2179cc265ff60"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "245ae10d-46cd-38ea-8829-68718d0cf8a5", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}